  ],
  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 1,
      "comment": "For pre-culturing, C. ljungdahlii was routinely grown in modified P7 medium in 160 mL serum bottles with a working volume of 10 mL at 35°C under a syngas headspace (Richter et al., 2013b)"
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "All chemicals were obtained from Sigma-Aldrich (St. Louis, MO, USA) except for syngas for which a blend of 60% (vol/vol) CO, 35% H2, and 5% CO2 was used (Airgas East, Ithaca, NY, USA)."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": "Bacteria were always grown anaerobically at 35 °C in medium designed for efficient syngas fermentation [22], which is referred to here as 1× medium."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 5,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": "P7 grows on CO, CO2, and H2. In addition to these gases, it can also utilize various sugars as a source of carbon for growth. The optimal pH range for survival and growth is between 5 and 6."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": "A defined medium containing minerals, trace metals, vitamins, and reducing agents was used to prepare the in- oculum and cultivate cells in the bioreactor."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": "The mineral stock solution contained (per liter) 80 g sodium chloride, 100 g ammonium chloride, 10 g potassium chloride, 10 g potassium monophosphate, 20 g magnesium sulfate, and 4 g calcium chloride."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 9,
      "comment": "The composition of stock solutions for trace metals and vitamins was previously described (Rajago- palan et al., 2002). The media contained (per liter) 30 mL mineral stock solution, 10 mL vitamin stock solution, 10 mL trace metal stock solution, 0.5 g yeast extract, 5 g morpholinoethanesulfonic acid (MES), and 5 mL of 4% cysteine-sulfide solution."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 10,
      "comment": "Resazurin solution (0.1 mL of 0.1%) was added as a redox indicator. Although the pH of the reactor was controlled using a pH controller, MES was added as a biological buffer to prevent excessive fluctua- tions in pH during the course of the experiment."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 11,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 12,
      "comment": "The vitamin stock solution contained (per liter) 10 mg pyridoxine, 5 mg each of thiamine, riboIavin, calcium pantothenate, thioctic acid, paraamino benzoic acid, nicotinic acid, and vitamin B12, and 2 mg each of d-biotin, folic acid, and 2-mercaptoethanesulfonic acid."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 13,
      "comment": "The trace metal stock solution contained (per liter) 2 g nitrilotriacetic acid, 1 g manganese sulfate, 0:8 g ferrous ammonium sulfate, 0:2 g cobalt chloride, 0:2 g zinc sulfate, and 20 mg each of cupric chloride, nickel chloride, sodium molybdate, sodium selenate, and sodium tungstate."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 14,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 16,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 18,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 20,
      "comment": ""
    }
  ]
}